# Regression pin for Gorget-arena snag #1: `String s = expr as String`
# followed by `s = s + ...` panicked at IR lowering with
#   Tier 2a consume-site violation: ... AssignIntoOwnedSlot(dst:
#   GorgetString) — untracked source consumed (ownership not decided).
#
# Two writer-site bugs combined to surface this:
#   (a) `src/ir/tag_ownership.rs` didn't tag `Instruction::Cast` dsts as
#       Owned, so a Cast-produced GorgetString stayed Untracked and the
#       very next bare-assign Move tripped the AssignIntoOwnedSlot
#       validator.
#   (b) `src/lir/lower/insts.rs`'s Cast handler didn't recognise
#       `Constant::Str` as a string source (its `Constant`-arm only
#       covered scalar literals), so a `"literal" as String` fell into
#       the `gorget_int_to_str` fallback and cc rejected the
#       `Str → int64_t` mismatch.
#
# Both fixed at the writer per CLAUDE.md "Debugging heuristic — fix
# complexity as a signal of wrong layer".

void main():
    String s = "x" as String
    s = s + "y"
    print(s)
